2 Background
2.1 HNSW and Contiguous SIMD
HNSW maintains multi-layer proximity graphs [1]. Queries greedily descend with candidate
heap sizeef search, then extract top-kat the base layer. Distance kernels assume contigu-
ousf32slices (A VX2/NEON), so a non-contiguous focus set must either (i) repack selected
coordinates into a scratch buffer before scoring, or (ii) gather them directly via SIMD gather
loads.
