4 Masked-Distance HNSW: Design Space
We consider three traversal-level strategies for evaluating distance only over a focus subspaceF
during HNSW descent, plus two supporting mechanisms (a kernel choice and a recall-recovery
pass) that apply across all three. Table 1 fixes the naming used for the rest of the paper.
4.1 API Surface
Focus parameters ride inside the existing query body:
"focus": {
"dims": [...], "masked": true,
"mask_from_layer": 1, // M2/M3 hybrid cutoff
"verify": true, // optional full rescore
"alpha": 0.25 // M3 blend weight
}
Constraints mirror existing dense local-search paths: no quantization/turbo, no simultaneous
with dims explainedon masked paths, and fail-fast ifmask from layer,verify, oralphaare
set withoutmasked=true.
