4.2 M1 — Naive All-Layer Masking
Withmasked=trueand no cutoff, every HNSW comparison during descent uses only coordinates
inF. This is the cheapest semantic change to implement, and the one most likely to be tried
first — which is precisely why we report it as a cautionary baseline rather than a proposal:
it destroys navigability whenever the focus metric disagrees with the full-space geometry the
graph was built on (Section 5.3).
4.3 M2 — Hybrid Layer Cutoff
Layerℓuses the masked scorer iffℓ < Lfor cutoffL=mask from layer; otherwise full
distance is used.L= 0 recovers plain (unmasked) nearest search; a largeLrecovers M1. The
implementation builds dual raw scorers insideFilteredScorerand switches viaset layerat
layer boundaries — visited-set and heap logic are unchanged, so this composes with the rest of
the query pipeline for free.
4.4 M3 — Weighted Blend
On masked layers, score =α·s full + (1−α)·s focus; coarse (unmasked) layers are unaffected.
Note that blending computesbothdistances, so it cannot reduce arithmetic cost on its own —
it exists purely as a routing-bias ablation to test whether it recovers recall at a fixed cutoff more
cheaply than raisingL.
4.5 Kernel Choice: Repack vs. Gather
Masked scoring can copy focus dims into a contiguous scratch buffer before calling the existing
SIMD kernels (repack), or gather them directly in-register (A VX2vgatherdpsfor Dot/Cosine/Euclidean
on x86, scalar fallback elsewhere). We add the gather path, selectable viaXQDRANT MASKED KERNEL,
and treat kernel choice as orthogonal to M1–M3: any of the three can use either kernel.
4.6 Verify and Overfetch
verify=truere-scores returned candidates with full distance after traversal, reusing the existing
quantization-rescore hook. At overfetchm=1 (i.e.,limit=k) this only reorders a size-kset,
so Recall@kis provably unchanged — it is a correctness/ordering feature, not a recall-recovery
one. Overfetch withm >1 (limit=m·k, keep top-kafter full rescore) turns masked traversal
into a candidatefilterand can recover recall, at a latency cost we quantify in Section 5.7.
