5.2 Attribution and Focus Rescoring Are Not the Same Problem
Figure 2 showswith dims explainedpreserves the latency–recall frontier vs. vanilla Qdrant
atD=768 (Recall@10 gap<0.01). Figure 3 shows in-database attribution holds∼3.5 ms p50
acrossm∈ {1, . . . ,50}while post-query extraction sits near 7.8 ms (≈2.2×). This confirms
attribution as a clean systems win. But Figure 4 shows thatnearest.focusrescoring— the
natural first attempt at subspace search, using the same full-preselection machinery — yields
speedup<1 (0.84–0.87). Rescoring reduces the dimensionality of the arithmetic but not the
traversal it depends on. This negative result is what motivates attacking the traversal itself,
which is the subject of the rest of this section.
