5.7 Verify + Overfetch Trades Latency for Recall, Where Coherence Allows
Given that M2 cannot reach full-space recall on its own, can a post-traversal verification pass
close the gap? At overfetchm=1, masked and verified Recall@10 are identical, as predicted in
Section 4 — reordering a fixed candidate set cannot change which candidates it contains. At
m=8 on SIFT with hybridL=1 (high coherence regime), full-space recall rises substantially:
0.26→0.66 at ratio 0.5 and 0.45→0.89 at ratio 0.75 (Figure 12), but at a cost of roughly
+45 ms p50 (∼1.5 ms→ ∼46 ms) — overfetching by 8×and fully rescoring is not cheap. On
high-Dsynthetic data (low coherence), recall stays≤∼0.19 even atm=8: exactly the outcome
Section 5.6 predicts, since no amount of overfetch recovers neighbors that the subspace metric
never surfaces as candidates in the first place.
